 "text": "Hi! How are you holding up? Wet wood burns fewer sparks, so if you can get it dry a day or two, it really improves the campfire. Fill them up with air out of the bag, squeeze them tightly several times, then drop one in middle. It makes great pop. Put them in right at the start, after each piece of wood. Start small enough off a rock so it's easy to extinguish. A small teapot and few tea cups are a nice basic set. Keep them above the fire to lug them up after each use. Rub it out with a handful of sand, then blow until the smoke stops. Then put the pot of water on it for few minutes.",
